\ A deep non-tail recursion compiled into the binary. Every level is a direct call between compiled
\ words, so the entry check each compiled word makes is the only guard that sees the native stack.
\ It raises a catchable error where the binary used to die on a signal.
\
\ The handler reports only that it ran, since reading the error type needs a native the
\ interpreter-free class cannot compile. The integration twins pin the type.

deep: stack-recursive ( n -- n ) [ dup 0 > [ 1 - deep 1 + ] [ ] if ] ;

[ 1000000 deep drop ] [ drop "caught the overflow" print-line ] recover
